<task id="041" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Mount `&lt;EmailComposer />` for email compose + Form Component Control swap (standard form retained as admin fallback)</title>
    <phase>Wave 4 — Channel-aware Communication Code Page</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>6</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>020, 040</dependencies>
    <blocks>043</blocks>
    <tags>code-page, dataverse</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Wires the shared-lib `&lt;EmailComposer />` engine into the Code Page (`.tsx`) and performs a Form Component Control swap changing default record-open behavior for `sprk_communication`; ADR-026/028/012/021 apply; FULL Step 9.5 gates required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-16</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Mount the canonical `&lt;EmailComposer />` engine (from task 020, `@spaarke/ui-components`) into the channel-aware Communication Code Page's **email** layout branch (task 040's interactive-email seam), then perform the **Form Component Control swap** so navigating to a `sprk_communication` record opens this Code Page instead of the auto-generated Dataverse standard form. The standard OOB form is **retained as a hidden / admin-only fallback** (reversibility — do NOT delete it).

    The composer is the channel-specific renderer mounted by the page for `sprk_communicationtype == Email`. Use the `&lt;SendEmailPage />` wrapper (mount='page') per reference §5.1.1, driven by the `mode` + `id` URL parameters parsed in task 040. Wire the URL contract per reference §7 exactly (compose | view | reply | forward | draft).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke front-end + Dataverse customization engineer. Fluent UI v9 + React 19 Code Pages + `@spaarke/ui-components` consumer. Knows the Form Component Control registration pattern and how to retain a fallback form for reversibility.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The Communication Code Page's email branch mounts `&lt;SendEmailPage mode={modeFromUrl} communicationId={idFromUrl} authenticatedFetch={...} bffBaseUrl={...} associations={...} onSent={...} onClose={...} />`. All five modes (compose/view/reply/forward/draft) resolve from the URL contract and render correctly. The `sprk_communication` main form is swapped to a Form Component Control hosting this Code Page as the default user-visible form; the standard auto-generated form is retained as an admin/debug fallback (not deleted). Build is clean via `npm run build:prod`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 040 built the channel-aware shell with a stubbed interactive-email seam. Task 020 (W2) built the canonical `&lt;EmailComposer />` engine + `SendEmailStep`/`SendEmailDialog`/`SendEmailPage` wrappers in `@spaarke/ui-components`. This task connects the two and makes the Code Page the default `sprk_communication` form.

      Per reference §7.4, the Form Component Control (Surface 2) is the higher-risk entry point because it changes default record-open behavior. The standard form MUST remain available as a fallback (NFR-07 reversibility / design decision 2026-06-05).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/code-pages/CommunicationPage/src/index.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/wrappers/SendEmailPage.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/index.ts</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/reference/r3-send-side-design.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">FR-16: mount the channel-specific composer for email compose via the `&lt;SendEmailPage />` wrapper; layout stays keyed on `sprk_communicationtype`, not "email" string.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Retain the standard OOB `sprk_communication` form as a hidden/admin fallback — do NOT delete it (reversibility, design decision 2026-06-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">URL contract per reference §7.3/§7.5 exactly: `mode` (compose|view|reply|forward|draft), `id`, pre-fill params, `associatedTo`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Consume `&lt;EmailComposer />`/`&lt;SendEmailPage />` from `@spaarke/ui-components`; do NOT fork or reimplement.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Inject `authenticatedFetch` + `bffBaseUrl` (host only, no `/api`) into the wrapper per props; no direct `@spaarke/auth` import inside shared-lib components.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-026">Standalone Code Page hosted via Form Component Control; single self-contained HTML artifact.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 page-mount visual variant per reference §5.10 (first-class entity-form look).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build with `npm run build:prod`; `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-solution-r4/reference/r3-send-side-design.md</file>
