  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The Code Page email branch mounts `&lt;SendEmailPage />` from `@spaarke/ui-components` (grep confirms no forked composer).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All five modes (compose/view/reply/forward/draft) resolve from the URL `mode` param and render the correct composer state.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`associatedTo` URL param maps to `associations` passed to the wrapper.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Non-email `sprk_communicationtype` values do NOT mount the composer (remain read-only from task 040).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A Form Component Control hosting the Code Page is registered as the default `sprk_communication` form.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The standard OOB form still exists (hidden/admin) — verifiable in the solution; not deleted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build:prod` produces a single self-contained artifact.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Deploy + UI tests are task 043. This task lands the wiring + FCC registration; smoke observations feed 043's `&lt;ui-tests&gt;`.

    Reversibility is a hard requirement — the standard form is the escape hatch if the FCC swap misbehaves. Record the exact form identifiers so 043/rollback can flip back without guesswork.
  </notes>

